{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ZEC",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I lifted up my eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said to me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its breadth, and what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its length.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I, saith the LORD, will be to her a wall of fire on every side, and will be the glory in the midst of her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ho, ho, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "come forth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deliver thyself, O Zion, that dwellest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the daughter of Babylon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me to the nations which wasted you: for he that toucheth you, toucheth the apple of his eye.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For behold, I will shake my hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing, and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And many nations shall be joined to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of thee, and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Jerusalem again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEC.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEC.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
